content.text:
We can rewrite these methods via generating smali from Java. Let's set up a small Java source with the new class containing all needed methods (including drawHudButton and icons preserved — but we don't want to rewrite whole class manually; we can compile just new versions of aboveRadarRect, applyFont, init, typeface, plus new fitRadar). Compile a class `DuneSegaHudPatch` in package com.ahsim.demulation with static methods, dex it, baksmali it, then extract method bodies and adapt register names to fit DuneSegaHud. Easier: create a full replacement Java class for DuneSegaHud with all methods (copy existing Java source, modify), compile with javac/d8, decode to smali, and replace the whole DuneSegaHud.smali. Need ensure method signatures match all call sites (aboveRadarRect, applyFont, drawHudButton, init, typeface). drawBaseIcon/drawUnitsIcon private. That is feasible. Use Android jar for compile. Then d8 to classes.dex, apktool decode to smali, copy resulting smali file. Need check d8 available: `$ANDROID_HOME/build-tools/34.0.0/d8`. Yes.

Let's write new Java class:

```java
package com.ahsim.demulation;
import android.content.Context;
import android.graphics.*;

public final class DuneSegaHud {
  private static Typeface cachedTypeface;
  private static boolean typefaceLoaded;
  private DuneSegaHud(){}

  public static Typeface typeface(Context c){
    if (cachedTypeface != null) return cachedTypeface;
    Typeface tf = Typeface.MONOSPACE;
    try {
      if (c != null) {
        Typeface custom = Typeface.createFromAsset(c.getAssets(), "fonts/dune_sega.ttf");
        if (custom != null) tf = custom;
      }
    } catch (Throwable ignored) {}
    cachedTypeface = tf;
    return tf;
  }
  public static void init(Context c){ typeface(c); }
  public static void applyFont(Paint p){ if(p==null) return; p.setTypeface(typeface(null)); p.setFakeBoldText(false); }

  // fixed layout in device pixels, three equal square buttons above radar
  public static void fitRadar(RectF viewport, RectF radar, float margin) {...}
  public static void aboveRadarRect(RectF radar, float scale, int slot, RectF out) {...}
  ...
}
```

Need `fitRadar` called from drawGenesisHud after radar set. But `drawGenesisHud` has `.locals 24`; calling static helper with 3 args doesn't need new registers if we reuse existing v-registers. We can insert:
```
