We can use Chromium to composite: load the user's screenshot as background image in an HTML page of size 2412x1080, overlay three square buttons and radar frame at computed positions, plus a version banner. That would be a "before/after" preview based on real gameplay screenshot. But careful: user asked screenshot at end. We can produce `site/preview/game_pro_preview.png` that uses the real gameplay frame with corrected HUD overlay. It's not a real in-game capture of our APK, but visually shows the result; we should label honestly maybe "PRO preview". Hmm previously we made a fully synthetic preview and user was unhappy about lack of actual changes. Now changes are real in APK. The preview can be illustrative.

Better approach: use the user's actual screenshot as base and crop/overlay the corrected buttons. The existing screenshot has radar cut off at bottom right; we can draw a correctly placed radar square at x=2110,y=778? Wait image is 2412x1080; our radar anchored to viewport bottom-right with 16px margin: viewport presumably full screen 2412x1080 => radar x=2110..2396, y=778..1064. But status bar may reduce viewport; close enough. Buttons row: 90px squares with 8px gaps, right-aligned at 2396, bottom at 762 -> x: 2110,2208,2306? Let's compute: size=286/3.18=89.94; right=2396; column0 left=2396-89.94=2306; column1 left=2396-2*89.94-8=2208; column2 left=2396-3*89.94-16=2110. So ordering: slot2 (third button) leftmost, slot1 (base) middle, slot0 (grouping) rightmost. Might want grouping leftmost for logic? User didn't specify order, just same size and above radar. But "кнопки юнитов и базы над радаром" — maybe group button left, base middle, third right. Our mapping puts grouping at right. We can invert columns so slot0 leftmost: `left = radar.right - size - (2-column)*(size+gap)`? Let's think: slot0 should be leftmost x=2110, slot1 x=2208, slot2 x=2306. Formula: left = radar.right - size - (2 - slot%3)*(size+gap). For slot0: right-size-2*(size+gap)=2396-90-196=2110. slot1: 2396-90-98=2208. slot2: 2396-90=2306. Good. Let's adjust helper to that ordering. It's more natural: grouping (units) left, base middle, third right.

Need update Java source, recompile, regenerate smali, replace, rebuild. Let's do that. Also maybe buttons should be exactly 90x90: size = radar.width()/3.18 = 89.94; fine. Could use `(radar.width() - 16)/3` = 90 exactly. Let's use that: size=(radar.width()-16f)/3f => (286-16)/3=90. gap=8. Then row width = 3*90+2*8=286 exactly. Great. Update Java:
```
float size=(radar.width()-16f)/3f;
if(size<48) size=48; if(size>96) size=96;
float gap=8f;
int column=slot%3;
float left=radar.right - size - (2-column)*(size+gap);
```
That yields exact alignment with radar width. Good.

